ike it. You don't have to change what you privately think. But for your own sake, and for the sake of the women you're trying to protect, handle this one by the book. Not because the book is morally pure, but because the book keeps you out of court and keeps the focus on actual misconduct, if there is any. That's common sense. The kind that comes from seeing good managers get ruined by acting on "what everyone knows." Don't be that manager.
